---
title: Braised Korean potatoes
servings: 4
tags: [korean]
cuisine: korean
time: 45 minutes
source: Braised potatoes by Andy Cooks, https://www.andy-cooks.com/blogs/recipes/braised-potatoes
nutrition:
  calories: 420 kcal
---

Heat the @olive oil{2%tbsp}(or lard) in a large #frying pan{} over medium-high heat.

Add the @red potatoes{1%kg}(baby) and season with @sea salt{}. Fry, tossing often, ~{10-15%minutes} until golden and crisp.

Stir in the @garlic{5%cloves}(finely grated), @soy sauce{1/3%cup}, @rice wine vinegar{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{2%tbsp} and @chicken stock{1%cup}(250 ml). Bring to a boil, then turn down to a simmer.

Cover and simmer ~{10%minutes}.

Uncover and stir in the @honey{2%tbsp}, @toasted sesame seeds{2%tsp} and @sesame oil{2%tsp}. Keep simmering, spooning the sauce over the potatoes, about ~{10%minutes} until the sauce is thick and glossy.

Stir in the whites of the @spring onions{2}(thinly sliced, whites and greens kept apart). Serve in a large bowl with the greens scattered over.
